The chocolate cake is fantastic, but very sweet.
Now I am very thirsty.
I would like to drink something.
The waiter walks past my table.
I look at him.
"Excuse me!" I say politely.
The waiter stops.
"Yes, please?" he asks in a friendly way.
"Could I please have a bottle of water?" I ask.
"Sparkling, please."
"Gladly," the waiter answers.
He goes briefly to the counter.
He comes back very quickly.
He brings a small bottle and a glass.
He puts the water on my table.
"Here you go," he says.
"Thank you very much," I answer.
I pour the water into the glass.
I take a sip.
The cold water is exactly right.
